title: Genesis 15 – Abram Believed God
description: A study in Genesis 15: the word of the LORD came to Abram, he believed and it was counted to him for righteousness, the covenant of the pieces, and the promise fulfilled in Christ.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-15-abram-believed-god.html

=== Introduction
--- Abram Believed God [title]
overline: A study in Genesis 15
sub: Counted for righteousness, and the promise fulfilled in Christ.
refs: Genesis 15:6
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== The word of the Lord
--- The word came to Abram in a vision
heading: The word of the {Lord} came
scripture: Genesis 15:1 | mark: Fear not, Abram: I am thy shield, and thy exceeding great reward
big: John 1:1-2
center: The Bible tells us who the word of God is. It is Jesus. [[John 1:14]]

--- Lord God, what wilt thou give me?
heading: {Lord} God, what wilt thou give me?
scripture: Genesis 15:2-5 | mark: he that shall come forth out of thine own bowels shall be thine heir; So shall thy seed be
p: Abram, old when he called upon the name of the {Lord} and received blessings and promises, now even older and without a true heir, questions the {Lord}. His faith tested, the word of God brings him forth to number the stars.

--- Counted for righteousness [title]
overline: Genesis 15:6
big: Genesis 15:6 | mark: he believed in the LORD; counted it to him for righteousness

--- Not of works
scripture: Romans 4:1-5 | mark: to him that worketh not, but believeth
big: James 2:23
p: The promise was made when *he believed in the {Lord}; and he counted it to him for righteousness*. His righteousness was imputed for that faith, by a gracious God. And it was faith in that seed to be given by the {Lord}. [[lesson:post-abraham-justified-by-faith-james-2|Abraham and James 2]]

=== The seed of Abraham
--- Even as Abraham believed God
scripture: Galatians 3:6-9 | mark: they which are of faith, the same are the children of Abraham; preached before the gospel unto Abraham
scripture: Galatians 3:16 | mark: And to thy seed, which is Christ

--- The law cannot disannul it
scripture: Galatians 3:17-18 | mark: four hundred and thirty years after, cannot disannul
scripture: Galatians 3:24-26
center: “And if ye be Christ’s, then are ye Abraham’s seed, and heirs according to the promise.” [[Galatians 3:29]]

--- As the stars of heaven
lead: We see in scripture that this promise was kept, his seed being one, Jesus Christ. And in Him the promise of a nation innumerable, like the stars in the sky, is fulfilled in Revelation 7.
scripture: Revelation 7:9-10 | mark: a great multitude, which no man could number, of all nations
p: Following the tribulation and the rapture, there are saints redeemed in the blood of Christ: 144,000 Old Testament saints, 12,000 from each of the tribes listed (not Jews, but Israelites), and *a great multitude, which no man could number, of all nations, and kindreds, and people, and tongues*. [[1 Thessalonians 4:16-17]] [[Revelation 7:4]]

--- The promise to Abraham
callout: This is the promise to Abraham. Not for the modern Jew. Not for the apostate and wicked modern state calling itself Israel. But of Christ and Him crucified, with the power to make the elect heirs to the Kingdom of Heaven: whosoever will call upon the name of the {Lord}.
center: Old Testament. New Testament. The same dispensation. The same promise. The same faith. [[Hebrews 11:39-40]]

--- They do not understand what they affirm
p: Dispensationalist Christians who say “God doesn’t break His promises!” don’t understand what the promises are, and don’t believe they are fulfilled in Christ. They cannot rightly divide the word of God, for whatever reason, and they allow wicked men with a Satanic agenda to tell them what it all means.
panel-warn: Knots | They twist themselves into knots trying to square the wicked doctrines of different paths to righteousness, one of works, one of blood, one of faith; the wicked doctrine of the pre-trib rapture; the invention that the millennial Kingdom is for the modern Jew.
refs: 1 Timothy 1:7

=== The covenant of the pieces
--- Whereby shall I know?
scripture: Genesis 15:7-11 | mark: whereby shall I know that I shall inherit it
p: The word of God tells him to offer an heifer, a she goat and a ram of three years old, a turtledove and a young pigeon. Each a sign or a picture of Christ, as established in the Levitical laws 400 years and more from when this is happening, to show the mercy of God in redemption by faith: the blood offerings, the sin offerings, the burnt offerings. A testament necessitates a blood offering. These were a symbol of Christ’s. [[Hebrews 9:16-22]]

--- A stranger in a land not theirs
scripture: Genesis 15:12-14 | mark: thy seed shall be a stranger in a land that is not theirs; four hundred years
p: In a deep sleep, a horror of great darkness fell upon Abram, and the word of God prophesied the sojourning in Egypt and enslavement. *And also that nation, whom they shall serve, will I judge: and afterward shall they come out with great substance.* Moses writing in the Spirit the prophecy of Exodus given to Abraham. [[Exodus 12:40-41]]

--- The iniquity of the Amorites
scripture: Genesis 15:15-16 | mark: the iniquity of the Amorites is not yet full
p: Abram himself will die knowing peace, but the land will not be given unto his descendants until the wickedness of the Amorites comes in. They are going to purge the land of Canaan of the wicked, as an instrument of the {Lord}. [[Leviticus 18:24-25]]
refs: Genesis 15:19-21

--- A burning lamp
scripture: Genesis 15:17-18 | mark: a smoking furnace, and a burning lamp that passed between those pieces
center: A furnace and a lamp passing between the pieces of the offering: a testament signed by God.

--- From the river of Egypt to Euphrates
lead: The Jews, so-called, will today say they rightly own “Greater Israel,” from the river to the sea, citing Genesis 15:18. From the Red Sea to the Euphrates, including Syria, parts of Jordan, Saudi Arabia and Iraq. They claim it is their birthright, to be secured by whatever means necessary.
callout: **But that’s not for them.** [[Revelation 21:1-3]]
scripture: Revelation 21:22-27 | mark: they which are written in the Lamb’s book of life

=== The reprobate doctrine
--- Full of iniquity
lead: One of the most important doctrines, which touches both the spiritual nature of man and a warning to heed here on earth, is the reprobate doctrine. It is taught throughout both the Old and New Testament.
p: Reprobation, the final and utter rejection by God of those who have finally and utterly rejected His overtures of grace, the call to Christ and the prodding and patience of the Holy Ghost, is one of the three spiritual states of man. [[Romans 1:28]] [[Jeremiah 6:30]]

--- The three spiritual states of man
panel: The unregenerate sinner | Dead in spirit but with the conscience of God within, who until death could hear the call and believe on Jesus Christ and be saved. The children of disobedience. [[Ephesians 2:1-3]]
panel: The saved | Those who call upon the name of the {Lord}, believing God’s testimony, spirit quickened. Born again believers, called the sons of God. [[John 1:12]]
panel-warn: The reprobate | Twice dead. Conscience seared. Hearts hardened, ears dulled. Unable to come to the knowledge of the truth. Rejected of God, given up. Clouds without water. The children of the devil. [[Jude 1:12-13]] [[1 Timothy 4:2]] [[2 Timothy 3:7-8]]

--- Lumped in with the common sinner
p: Often Christians, seeking to be kind and show mercy, thinking they are doing the right thing, will completely ignore the final group, lumping them in with the common sinner. Holding out hope, even when they reveal their wickedness in ways exactly as God’s word tells us they will.
p: Evil often isn’t an outward appearance of malevolence, like a comic book super villain. It’s often someone who is a miserable human being. We take pity on them, and they use our good-natured inclination for mercy and grace to take advantage of us. They are the false teachers, the false prophets bringing doctrines of damnation, with the appearance of holiness, whited sepulchres. [[Matthew 23:27-33]] [[2 Peter 2:1]]
note: Study the whole doctrine in [[lesson:topic-reprobate|The Reprobate Mind]], to better defend yourself, your family and your community.

=== Close
--- The same promise, the same faith [title]
overline: Genesis 15
point: The Word came to Abram | Fear not: I am thy shield, and thy exceeding great reward.
point: He believed | And it was counted to him for righteousness, without works.
point: The seed is Christ | Heirs as the stars, a great multitude of all nations, in Him.
point: God’s timing | The iniquity of the Amorites was not yet full. God judges in His time.

